<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where each block <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{1},...,Q_{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{1},...,Q_{16}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L/4\times d/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L/4\times d/4</annotation></semantics></math> submatrix, each block <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{1},...,K_{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{1},...,K_{16}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/4\times L/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/4\times L/4</annotation></semantics></math>, and each block <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1},...,S_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1},...,S_{10}</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L/4\times L/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L/4\times L/4</annotation></semantics></math> submatrix.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm 1 computes <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> full matrix multiplications (<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1},...,m_{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1},...,m_{24}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications that only require lower-triangular half of the result (<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},...,h_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},...,h_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>). This leads to a total complexity of</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24\cdot\left(\frac{L}{4}\right)^{2}\cdot\left(\frac{d}{4}\right)+\frac{1}{2}\cdot 10\cdot\left(\frac{L}{4}\right)^{2}\cdot\left(\frac{d}{4}\right)=\frac{29}{64}L^{2}d\approx 0.453L^{2}d\qquad({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bf 9.4\%}\downarrow}\text{ vs }0.5L^{2}d)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>L</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>29</mn><mn>64</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>0.453</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathvariant="bold">9.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mtext> vs </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24\cdot\left(\frac{L}{4}\right)^{2}\cdot\left(\frac{d}{4}\right)+\frac{1}{2}\cdot 10\cdot\left(\frac{L}{4}\right)^{2}\cdot\left(\frac{d}{4}\right)=\frac{29}{64}L^{2}d\approx 0.453L^{2}d\qquad({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bf 9.4\%}\downarrow}\text{ vs }0.5L^{2}d),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which is a <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 9.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>9.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 9.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> reduction to the standard algorithm (computing lower-triangular half of the matrix product <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="QK^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">QK^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>). Using recursive calls for <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},...,h_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},...,h_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can obtain a further theoretical reduction to</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{4}{9}L^{2}d\approx 0.444L^{2}d\qquad({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bf 11.1\%}\downarrow}\text{ vs }0.5L^{2}d)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>0.444</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathcolor="#FF0000" mathvariant="bold">11.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mrow><mtext> vs </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{4}{9}L^{2}d\approx 0.444L^{2}d\qquad({\color[rgb]{1,0,0}{\bf 11.1\%}\downarrow}\text{ vs }0.5L^{2}d).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">In practice, the use of recursion is optional, and the decision is left to the practitioner.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>FCA Stage II: Multiplying the Attention Scores by the Value Matrix</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we view the matrices <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{rowSoftmax(S/\sqrt{d})}=P\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>rowSoftmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rowSoftmax(S/\sqrt{d})}=P\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as well as the output <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O=PV\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O=PV\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> as block matrices</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}P_{1}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
P_{2}&amp;P_{3}&amp;0&amp;0\\
P_{4}&amp;P_{5}&amp;P_{6}&amp;0\\
P_{7}&amp;P_{8}&amp;P_{9}&amp;P_{10}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}V_{1}&amp;V_{2}&amp;V_{3}&amp;V_{4}\\
V_{5}&amp;V_{6}&amp;V_{7}&amp;V_{8}\\
V_{9}&amp;V_{10}&amp;V_{11}&amp;V_{12}\\
V_{13}&amp;V_{14}&amp;V_{15}&amp;V_{16}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}O_{1}&amp;O_{2}&amp;O_{3}&amp;O_{4}\\
O_{5}&amp;O_{6}&amp;O_{7}&amp;O_{8}\\
O_{9}&amp;O_{10}&amp;O_{11}&amp;O_{12}\\
O_{13}&amp;O_{14}&amp;O_{15}&amp;O_{16}\end{pmatrix}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>P</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>13</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>15</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>V</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>6</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>8</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>9</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>11</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>12</mn></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>13</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>14</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>15</mn></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>16</mn></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}P_{1}&amp;0&amp;0&amp;0\\
P_{2}&amp;P_{3}&amp;0&amp;0\\
P_{4}&amp;P_{5}&amp;P_{6}&amp;0\\
P_{7}&amp;P_{8}&amp;P_{9}&amp;P_{10}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}V_{1}&amp;V_{2}&amp;V_{3}&amp;V_{4}\\
V_{5}&amp;V_{6}&amp;V_{7}&amp;V_{8}\\
V_{9}&amp;V_{10}&amp;V_{11}&amp;V_{12}\\
V_{13}&amp;V_{14}&amp;V_{15}&amp;V_{16}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}O_{1}&amp;O_{2}&amp;O_{3}&amp;O_{4}\\
O_{5}&amp;O_{6}&amp;O_{7}&amp;O_{8}\\
O_{9}&amp;O_{10}&amp;O_{11}&amp;O_{12}\\
O_{13}&amp;O_{14}&amp;O_{15}&amp;O_{16}\end{pmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Algorithm 2 computes the output <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> using <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math> full matrix multiplications (<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1},...,m_{24}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>24</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1},...,m_{24}</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> multiplications (<math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1},...,h_{10}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>10</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1},...,h_{10}</annotation></semantics></math>) where first matrix is non-zero only in the lower half. Therefore, the complexity analysis shows the same improvements of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 9.4\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>9.4</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 9.4\%</annotation></semantics></math> without recursion and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx 11.1\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mn>11.1</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 11.1\%</annotation></semantics></math> with recursion.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We would like to emphasize the relative simplicity of the expressions that appear in Algorithm 2. First, all expressions have at most <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> terms, except <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{7},m_{10},m_{13}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mn>13</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{7},m_{10},m_{13}</annotation></semantics></math>. Second, half of <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are used exactly once (in contrast to Strassen algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Strassen, 1969</a>)</cite>), which means that they do not require storage in different parts of memory and can directly accumulate in the final output <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>O</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives hope that there exist simpler alternatives to Algorithm 2.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">It is worth noting that Algorithm 2 has other applications in High Performance Computing, e.g. in solution of Generalized Symmetric Eigenvalue problem using Cholesky decomposition. In this setup, we want to solve the equation</p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ax=\lambda Bx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ax=\lambda Bx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">After Cholesky decomposition of <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=LL^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=LL^{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can do change of variable <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=L^{-T}y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=L^{-T}y</annotation></semantics></math>, to get</p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="AL^{-T}y=\lambda Ly\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad L^{-1}AL^{-T}y=\lambda y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AL^{-T}y=\lambda Ly\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad L^{-1}AL^{-T}y=\lambda y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The expression <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{-1}AL^{-T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{-1}AL^{-T}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed either by sequential backward substitution, or by two matrix multiplications. Each of the two matrix multiplications can benefit from Algorithm 2.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Forward and Backward Pass in Causal Attention</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Applying row permutations, column permutations, and transpositions to Algorithm 1 and Algorithm 2, we effortlessly obtain reductions for matrix product</p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB=C," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB=C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where any single of the matrices <math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,B,C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,B,C</annotation></semantics></math> is upper-triangular or lower-triangular.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A closer inspection of forward and backward pass in causal attention reveals that all performed matrix multiplications have the structure described above. In each case, we highlight the upper-triangular or lower-triangular matrix in red.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="--ltx-border-color:#000000;padding:9.0pt;">
        
<div id="S2.SS3.2.1" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Pass</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="S2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="S2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<ol id="S2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}S}=\mathrm{Mask}(QK^{T})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Mask</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}S}=\mathrm{Mask}(QK^{T})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=\mathrm{rowSoftmax}(S/\sqrt{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rowSoftmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=\mathrm{rowSoftmax}(S/\sqrt{d})\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P}V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P}V\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
        
</div>
        
<div id="S2.SS3.2.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;">
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Backward Pass</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> <math id="S2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q,K,V,dO\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},P\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q,K,V,dO\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d},P\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
          
<div id="S2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> <math id="S2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dQ,dK,dV\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dQ,dK,dV\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<ol id="S2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dV={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P^{T}}dO\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dV={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}P^{T}}dO\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dP}=dOV^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">P</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dP}=dOV^{T}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dS=d\mathrm{rowSoftmax}(dP)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>rowSoftmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dS=d\mathrm{rowSoftmax}(dP)\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dQ={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dS}K\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dQ={\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dS}K\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">5.</span> 
<div id="S2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dK=Q{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dS^{T}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dK=Q{\color[rgb]{1,0,0}dS^{T}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="S2.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;"> <math id="S2.I2.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-10\%)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">%</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-10\%)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
